Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Future: The Component Bridge", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.976831838692709*^9, 3.976831872269437*^9}, 
   3.976834533852539*^9},ExpressionUUID->"37c3f9e4-cd1c-4914-897f-\
1f845139ea88"],

Cell["\<\
While this toolkit currently focuses on formalism (the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]glass box\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]), we intend \
eventually to integrate with Wolfram\[CloseCurlyQuote]s component-based \
tools. In future parts of this series, we plan a compiler backend that takes \
a validated \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] expression such as a derived \
geodesic equation and translates it into, for instance, Wolfram\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s native TensorContract and the function repository\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s MetricTensor. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9768318459260063`*^9, 3.976832082815949*^9}, {
  3.9768345409216146`*^9, 
  3.976834657396703*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ed79d245-8c0b-4631-afd0-\
47eea49df35b"],

Cell["\<\
This architecture positions \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] as a \
type-checked frontend, treating Wolfram\[CloseCurlyQuote]s tensor support as \
a target virtual machine. We aspire to give the physicist the best of many \
worlds: formal rigour during derivation, symbolical and numerical agility at \
the component level, and speed during numerical simulations.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9768318459260063`*^9, 3.976832082815949*^9}, {
  3.9768345409216146`*^9, 3.9768346823435917`*^9}, {3.976836518263199*^9, 
  3.976836519306658*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"11ae1b06-ccb5-450c-90f1-\
14dd267f1fb4"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

